## Context

The long paper explains observed country and project trajectories. Earlier absorption, instrument-substitution and national-ownership arguments are working hypotheses; the author asks to reimagine the paper to fit the data.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Parent tracker: 0725.

## First test

First claim-audit exercise: for one proposed mechanism, link each premise to a dated source, state a rival explanation and identify evidence that would disconfirm it. An inference presented as an observation or selected success case standing in for the portfolio must fail review.

## Actions

Rewrite conception/jetp-papier-long-economie-politique.md and the LaTeX manuscript in deliverables/jetp-econpol. Build a comparative evidence matrix on financial instruments, domestic institutions, negotiation and ownership arrangements; select cases transparently and include stalled or contradictory cases. Incorporate 0730 results when available without blocking initial case analysis. Coordinate the analytical framing with Christophe through the author; this ticket does not authorise sending messages. Keep construction, emissions and justice outcomes outside demonstrated claims unless directly evidenced.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Comparative argument grounded in frozen source-backed observations
- [ ] Mechanisms, rival explanations and negative cases explicit
- [ ] No predetermined absorption or substitution conclusion
- [ ] Connection to short-paper findings and limits stated without duplication
- [ ] Reviewable LaTeX manuscript and claim-evidence matrix for author/Christophe discussion

